  "review": {
    "comments": [
      {
        "id": 4051931757,
        "body": "**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Unwrap parenthesized PHP include paths**\n\nFor valid static imports such as `require('client.php')` or `include_once(\"config.php\")`, the operand is a `parenthesized_expression`, so passing it directly to `_literal` always returns `None`. These common forms therefore lose their import edge despite containing a static quoted path; unwrap a single parenthesized expression before applying the literal check.\n\nUseful? React with \ud83d\udc4d\u00a0/ \ud83d\udc4e.",
        "original_commit_id": "524b138c17b3aa0084337c9a61bea9ef94c97f79",
